Rem Capability: scribbler
Rem ==================================================================
Rem seedplotter.shoddy — reckoner seed: plotter.shoddy, a chart from
Rem the numbers you already have on the stack
Rem
Rem A session that has just computed a column of numbers is one word
Rem away from a histogram of them. That is the whole case for this seed:
Rem every other charting story starts with "now write a program".
Rem
Rem THE SIMPLEST OF THE RESOURCE SEEDS, and worth saying why. plotter's
Rem words take and return a SCRIBBLER — it has no state of its own at
Rem all, no position like a turtle's and no layout remembered between
Rem calls. So the binding is a scribbler slot and nothing else, exactly
Rem as seedscribbler's is, and RckUpdated never comes into it.
Rem
Rem ---- THE THREE ABORTS, AND THE FOUR THE MACHINE DOES NOT NAME -----
Rem
Rem plotter Errors three times: a histogram with no bins, a bar chart
Rem with a negative value, a pie chart with a value that is not
Rem positive. Each is pre-flighted here.
Rem
Rem It also aborts in four places it does not announce, and those are
Rem the ones worth finding before a session does. Minimum and Maximum of
Rem an EMPTY list have no answer, so every chart needs data; BarChart
Rem divides by the number of values, so an empty one divides by zero;
Rem and BarChart and PieChart both index labels by the value's position,
Rem so fewer labels than values reads past the end. A guard list that
Rem only covered the stated three would leave a session four ways to
Rem lose its work.
Rem
Rem ---- WHAT A CHART IS FOR, HERE ------------------------------------
Rem
Rem Each chart word draws onto the window and answers NOTHING, in the
Rem shape seedscribbler and seedturtle set: the session holds a name,
Rem not a surface, so there is nothing to drop. PLOTBLIT shows it and
Rem PLOTSAVE writes a PNG — and a session that has drawn and seen
Rem nothing has forgotten PLOTBLIT.
Rem
Rem THE CHARTS DRAW THEIR OWN AXES, so there is no PLOTAXES word: every
Rem one of the five calls DrawAxes itself, and a session that could draw
Rem axes separately could only draw them twice.
Rem ==================================================================

Include "plotter.shoddy"
Include "cuttle.shoddy"
Include "reckoner.shoddy"
Include "seq.shoddy"

Def PsKindName() As String
    "plotter"

Rem ---- finding the plot a word was named --------------------------------

Def PsFound(word As String, st As RckState, c As Cell) As Result
    Select Case RckTextArg(word, c)
        Case Ok(nm)
            PsFoundAt(word, st, nm)
        Case Err(w, at)
            Err(w, at)
        Case Else
            Err(word & " did not answer", 0)

Def PsFoundAt(word As String, st As RckState, nm As String) As Result
    If Not RckBoundTo(st, nm) Then
        Err(word & ": THERE IS NOTHING OPEN CALLED " & nm, 0)
    Else
        PsFoundKind(word, First(RckResOf(st, nm)), nm)

Def PsFoundKind(word As String, r As RckRes, nm As String) As Result
    If ResKindOf(r) <> PsKindName() Then
        Err(word & ": " & nm & " IS A " & Upper(ResKindOf(r)) & ", NOT A PLOT", 0)
    Else
        Ok(r)

Def PsWindow(r As RckRes) As Scribbler
    ScribblerOf(ResHandOf(r))

Rem ---- PLOTOPEN ----------------------------------------------------------

Def PsSeedOpen(st As RckState) As RckState
    Let s1 = RckReg(st, "PLOTOPEN", 3, RckPureOver(Fn(s, vs) => PsOpen(s, vs)), "( w h name -- )", "Open a w by h chart window, white, and keep it under that name. CLOSE shuts it; BOUND lists what is open. 640 by 480 is a comfortable size.")
    Let s2 = RckReg(s1, "PLOTTITLE", 2, RckPureOver(Fn(s, vs) => PsTitle(s, vs)), "( name s -- )", "Write s across the top of the chart.")
    Let s3 = RckReg(s2, "PLOTBLIT", 1, RckPureOver(Fn(s, vs) => PsBlit(s, vs)), "( name -- )", "Show what has been drawn. A chart nobody can see is one nobody blitted.")
    RckReg(s3, "PLOTSAVE", 2, RckPureOver(Fn(s, vs) => PsSave(s, vs)), "( name path -- ok )", "Write the chart to a PNG file; True on success, False on a path it cannot write.")

Def PsOpen(st As RckState, vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case Pair(RckWholeArg("PLOTOPEN", Nth(vs, 1)), RckWholeArg("PLOTOPEN", Nth(vs, 2)))
        Case Pair(Ok(wid), Ok(hgt))
            PsOpenNamed(st, wid, hgt, Nth(vs, 3))
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("PLOTOPEN needs a width, a height and a name")

Def PsOpenNamed(st As RckState, wid As Number, hgt As Number, nc As Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckTextArg("PLOTOPEN", nc)
        Case Ok(nm)
            PsOpenFree(st, wid, hgt, nm)
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("PLOTOPEN did not answer")

Def PsOpenFree(st As RckState, wid As Number, hgt As Number, nm As String) As RckWork
    If RckBoundTo(st, nm) Then
        RckWorkBad("PLOTOPEN: THERE IS ALREADY SOMETHING OPEN CALLED " & nm)
    Else
        PsOpenSized(wid, hgt, nm)

Rem The margins are fixed — 60 left, 40 top and so on — so a window much
Rem smaller than them has no plot area at all and every bar is drawn at a
Rem negative width. Refused with the smallest that works rather than left
Rem to come out as a blank rectangle.
Def PsOpenSized(wid As Number, hgt As Number, nm As String) As RckWork
    If wid < PsLeastWide() Or hgt < PsLeastTall() Then
        RckWorkBad("PLOTOPEN: A CHART NEEDS AT LEAST " & Str(PsLeastWide()) & " BY " & Str(PsLeastTall()) & " — THE MARGINS TAKE THE REST")
    Else
        PsOpenAt(wid, hgt, nm)

Rem The margins plus a plot area worth having. MarginLeft and the rest
Rem are plotter's own, so this moves with them.
Def PsLeastWide() As Number
    MarginLeft() + MarginRight() + 40

Def PsLeastTall() As Number
    MarginTop() + MarginBottom() + 40

Rem NewPlot goes through the ABORTING ScribblerOpen, so the window is
Rem opened through the guarded one and the white fill — the other half
Rem of what NewPlot does — is done here.
Def PsOpenAt(wid As Number, hgt As Number, nm As String) As RckWork
    Select Case TryScribblerOpen(wid, hgt)
        Case Ok(slot)
            PsOpenFilled(slot, nm, ScribblerFill(ScribblerOf(slot), 255, 255, 255))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad("PLOTOPEN: " & w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("PLOTOPEN did not answer")

Def PsOpenFilled(slot As Number, nm As String, sc As Scribbler) As RckWork
    RckOpened(nm, PsKindName(), slot, CutNum(0), Fn() => ScribblerShut(slot))

Rem ---- the words that are not charts -------------------------------------

Def PsTitle(st As RckState, vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case Pair(PsFound("PLOTTITLE", st, Nth(vs, 1)), RckTextArg("PLOTTITLE", Nth(vs, 2)))
        Case Pair(Ok(r), Ok(s))
            PsDrew(PlotTitle(PsWindow(r), s))
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("PLOTTITLE needs a name and a STRING")

Def PsBlit(st As RckState, vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case PsFound("PLOTBLIT", st, First(vs))
        Case Ok(r)
            PsDrew(ScribblerBlit(PsWindow(r)))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("PLOTBLIT did not answer")

Rem Every chart word ends here: the surface was mutated in place, so the
Rem Scribbler the machine threads back has nowhere to go and the session
Rem gets nothing rather than something to DROP.
Def PsDrew(sc As Scribbler) As RckWork
    RckVals({ })

Def PsSave(st As RckState, vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case Pair(PsFound("PLOTSAVE", st, Nth(vs, 1)), RckTextArg("PLOTSAVE", Nth(vs, 2)))
        Case Pair(Ok(r), Ok(path))
            PsSaveTo(r, path)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("PLOTSAVE needs a name and a path")

Def PsSaveTo(r As RckRes, path As String) As RckWork
    If Not TryWriteFile(path, "") Then
        RckVals({ CutBool(False) })
    Else
        PsSaved(ScribblerSave(PsWindow(r), path))

Def PsSaved(sc As Scribbler) As RckWork
    RckVals({ CutBool(True) })

Rem ---- reading a list of numbers off the stack ---------------------------

Def PsNums(word As String, c As Cell) As Result
    Select Case RckListArg(word, c)
        Case Ok(xs)
            PsNumsAt(word, xs, { })
        Case Err(w, at)
            Err(w, at)
        Case Else
            Err(word & " did not answer", 0)

Def PsNumsAt(word As String, xs As List Of Cell, acc As List Of Number) As Result
    If IsEmpty(xs) Then
        Ok(acc)
    Else
        PsNumsNext(word, xs, acc, First(xs))

Def PsNumsNext(word As String, xs As List Of Cell, acc As List Of Number, c As Cell) As Result
    Select Case c
        Case CutNum(x)
            PsNumsAt(word, Rest(xs), Append(acc, x))
        Case Else
            Err(RckKindWhy(word, "a LIST of NUMBERs", c), 0)

Def PsStrs(word As String, c As Cell) As Result
    Select Case RckListArg(word, c)
        Case Ok(xs)
            PsStrsAt(word, xs, { })
        Case Err(w, at)
            Err(w, at)
        Case Else
            Err(word & " did not answer", 0)

Def PsStrsAt(word As String, xs As List Of Cell, acc As List Of String) As Result
    If IsEmpty(xs) Then
        Ok(acc)
    Else
        PsStrsNext(word, xs, acc, First(xs))

Def PsStrsNext(word As String, xs As List Of Cell, acc As List Of String, c As Cell) As Result
    Select Case c
        Case CutStr(s)
            PsStrsAt(word, Rest(xs), Append(acc, s), )
        Case Else
            Err(RckKindWhy(word, "a LIST of STRINGs", c), 0)

Rem Minimum and Maximum of an empty list have no answer, and every chart
Rem reaches for one or both. This is the guard plotter does not state and
Rem the one a session would meet first.
Def PsWhyEmpty(word As String, xs As List Of Number) As String
    If IsEmpty(xs) Then
        word & ": THERE ARE NO NUMBERS TO PLOT"
    Else
        ""

Rem ---- PLOTHISTOGRAM ------------------------------------------------------

Def PsSeedCharts(st As RckState) As RckState
    Let s1 = RckReg(st, "PLOTHISTOGRAM", 3, RckPureOver(Fn(s, vs) => PsHist(s, vs)), "( name xs bins -- )", "Draw a histogram of xs in that many bins, with axes and labels. Refuses on no numbers or fewer than one bin.")
    Let s2 = RckReg(s1, "PLOTSCATTER", 3, RckPureOver(Fn(s, vs) => PsScatter(s, vs)), "( name xs ys -- )", "Draw xs against ys as points, with axes and labels. Refuses unless the two lists are the same length and neither is empty.")
    Let s3 = RckReg(s2, "PLOTBOX", 2, RckPureOver(Fn(s, vs) => PsBox(s, vs)), "( name xs -- )", "Draw a box plot of xs: quartiles, median, whiskers to 1.5 times the inter-quartile range, and outliers as dots.")
    Let s4 = RckReg(s3, "PLOTBAR", 3, RckPureOver(Fn(s, vs) => PsBar(s, vs)), "( name labels values -- )", "Draw a bar chart. Refuses unless there is one label per value and every value is 0 or more.")
    RckReg(s4, "PLOTPIE", 3, RckPureOver(Fn(s, vs) => PsPie(s, vs)), "( name labels values -- )", "Draw a pie chart with a legend. Refuses unless there is one label per value and every value is above 0 — a slice of nothing has no angle.")

Def PsHist(st As RckState, vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case Pair(PsFound("PLOTHISTOGRAM", st, Nth(vs, 1)), PsNums("PLOTHISTOGRAM", Nth(vs, 2)))
        Case Pair(Ok(r), Ok(xs))
            PsHistBins(r, xs, Nth(vs, 3))
        Case Else
            PsWhyPair("PLOTHISTOGRAM", st, vs)

Def PsHistBins(r As RckRes, xs As List Of Number, bc As Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckWholeArg("PLOTHISTOGRAM", bc)
        Case Ok(n)
            PsHistSound(r, xs, n)
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("PLOTHISTOGRAM did not answer")

Def PsHistSound(r As RckRes, xs As List Of Number, n As Number) As RckWork
    If PsWhyEmpty("PLOTHISTOGRAM", xs) <> "" Then
        RckWorkBad(PsWhyEmpty("PLOTHISTOGRAM", xs))
    Else
        PsHistBinned(r, xs, n)

Def PsHistBinned(r As RckRes, xs As List Of Number, n As Number) As RckWork
    If n < 1 Then
        RckWorkBad("PLOTHISTOGRAM: A HISTOGRAM NEEDS AT LEAST ONE BIN")
    Else
        PsDrew(Histogram(PsWindow(r), xs, n))

Rem ---- PLOTSCATTER ---------------------------------------------------------

Def PsScatter(st As RckState, vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case Pair(PsFound("PLOTSCATTER", st, Nth(vs, 1)), PsNums("PLOTSCATTER", Nth(vs, 2)))
        Case Pair(Ok(r), Ok(xs))
            PsScatterYs(r, xs, PsNums("PLOTSCATTER", Nth(vs, 3)))
        Case Else
            PsWhyPair("PLOTSCATTER", st, vs)

Def PsScatterYs(r As RckRes, xs As List Of Number, ys As Result) As RckWork
    Select Case ys
        Case Ok(yy)
            PsScatterPaired(r, xs, yy)
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("PLOTSCATTER did not answer")

Rem Zip stops at the shorter list, so unequal lengths would silently plot
Rem part of the data — a wrong chart rather than a refused one, which is
Rem the outcome worth the most trouble to prevent.
Def PsScatterPaired(r As RckRes, xs As List Of Number, ys As List Of Number) As RckWork
    If PsWhyEmpty("PLOTSCATTER", xs) <> "" Then
        RckWorkBad(PsWhyEmpty("PLOTSCATTER", xs))
    Else
        PsScatterSized(r, xs, ys)

Def PsScatterSized(r As RckRes, xs As List Of Number, ys As List Of Number) As RckWork
    If Length(xs) <> Length(ys) Then
        RckWorkBad("PLOTSCATTER: " & Str(Length(xs)) & " X VALUES AND " & Str(Length(ys)) & " Y VALUES — THEY MUST PAIR UP")
    Else
        PsDrew(ScatterPlot(PsWindow(r), xs, ys))

Rem ---- PLOTBOX -------------------------------------------------------------

Def PsBox(st As RckState, vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case Pair(PsFound("PLOTBOX", st, Nth(vs, 1)), PsNums("PLOTBOX", Nth(vs, 2)))
        Case Pair(Ok(r), Ok(xs))
            PsBoxSound(r, xs)
        Case Else
            PsWhyPair("PLOTBOX", st, vs)

Def PsBoxSound(r As RckRes, xs As List Of Number) As RckWork
    If PsWhyEmpty("PLOTBOX", xs) <> "" Then
        RckWorkBad(PsWhyEmpty("PLOTBOX", xs))
    Else
        PsDrew(BoxPlot(PsWindow(r), xs))

Rem ---- PLOTBAR and PLOTPIE -------------------------------------------------

Def PsBar(st As RckState, vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case Pair(PsFound("PLOTBAR", st, Nth(vs, 1)), PsStrs("PLOTBAR", Nth(vs, 2)))
        Case Pair(Ok(r), Ok(ls))
            PsBarVals(r, ls, PsNums("PLOTBAR", Nth(vs, 3)))
        Case Else
            PsWhyLabelled("PLOTBAR", st, vs)

Def PsBarVals(r As RckRes, ls As List Of String, ns As Result) As RckWork
    Select Case ns
        Case Ok(xs)
            PsBarChecked(r, ls, xs, PsWhyLabels("PLOTBAR", ls, xs))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("PLOTBAR did not answer")

Def PsBarChecked(r As RckRes, ls As List Of String, xs As List Of Number, why As String) As RckWork
    If why <> "" Then
        RckWorkBad(why)
    Else
        PsBarSigned(r, ls, xs)

Def PsBarSigned(r As RckRes, ls As List Of String, xs As List Of Number) As RckWork
    If Any(xs, Fn(x) => x < 0) Then
        RckWorkBad("PLOTBAR: EVERY VALUE MUST BE 0 OR MORE — A BAR BELOW THE AXIS HAS NOWHERE TO GO")
    Else
        PsDrew(BarChart(PsWindow(r), ls, xs))

Def PsPie(st As RckState, vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case Pair(PsFound("PLOTPIE", st, Nth(vs, 1)), PsStrs("PLOTPIE", Nth(vs, 2)))
        Case Pair(Ok(r), Ok(ls))
            PsPieVals(r, ls, PsNums("PLOTPIE", Nth(vs, 3)))
        Case Else
            PsWhyLabelled("PLOTPIE", st, vs)

Def PsPieVals(r As RckRes, ls As List Of String, ns As Result) As RckWork
    Select Case ns
        Case Ok(xs)
            PsPieChecked(r, ls, xs, PsWhyLabels("PLOTPIE", ls, xs))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("PLOTPIE did not answer")

Def PsPieChecked(r As RckRes, ls As List Of String, xs As List Of Number, why As String) As RckWork
    If why <> "" Then
        RckWorkBad(why)
    Else
        PsPieSigned(r, ls, xs)

Def PsPieSigned(r As RckRes, ls As List Of String, xs As List Of Number) As RckWork
    If Any(xs, Fn(x) => x <= 0) Then
        RckWorkBad("PLOTPIE: EVERY VALUE MUST BE ABOVE 0 — A SLICE OF NOTHING HAS NO ANGLE")
    Else
        PsDrew(PieChart(PsWindow(r), ls, xs))

Rem The two guards a labelled chart needs and plotter states neither of:
Rem an empty set divides by zero on its way to the bar width, and fewer
Rem labels than values indexes past the end of the labels.
Def PsWhyLabels(word As String, ls As List Of String, xs As List Of Number) As String
    If IsEmpty(xs) Then
        word & ": THERE ARE NO VALUES TO PLOT"
    Else
        PsWhyPaired(word, ls, xs)

Def PsWhyPaired(word As String, ls As List Of String, xs As List Of Number) As String
    If Length(ls) <> Length(xs) Then
        word & ": " & Str(Length(ls)) & " LABELS AND " & Str(Length(xs)) & " VALUES — THERE MUST BE ONE LABEL EACH"
    Else
        ""

Rem ---- saying which argument was wrong ------------------------------------

Rem A Pair match that failed says nothing about WHICH half failed, so the
Rem name is asked again on its own and its answer preferred: a mistyped
Rem name is the likeliest mistake and the one worth naming first.
Def PsWhyPair(word As String, st As RckState, vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case PsFound(word, st, Nth(vs, 1))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            PsWhyNums(word, PsNums(word, Nth(vs, 2)))

Def PsWhyNums(word As String, r As Result) As RckWork
    Select Case r
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad(word & " needs a name and a LIST of NUMBERs")

Def PsWhyLabelled(word As String, st As RckState, vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case PsFound(word, st, Nth(vs, 1))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            PsWhyStrs(word, PsStrs(word, Nth(vs, 2)))

Def PsWhyStrs(word As String, r As Result) As RckWork
    Select Case r
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad(word & " needs a name, a LIST of STRINGs and a LIST of NUMBERs")

Rem ---- the seed ------------------------------------------------------------

Def RckSeedPlotter(st As RckState) As RckState
    Let s1 = PsSeedOpen(RckSeeding(st, "seed-plotter"))
    PsSeedCharts(s1)
